WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:07.899
Speaker 1: It is so obvious that former Republican
New Jersey Governor Chris Christie is by far

00:00:07.899 --> 00:00:12.160
the best Republican candidate running for
president this year.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.010
He is, at least for now, not doing the anti-woke
stuff.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:23.170
He's willing to go after failed twice, impeached
once indicted former President Donald Trump.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:29.050
He sounds like a normal person, although we
obviously have policy disagreements and the

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.759
MAGA people don't want him.

00:00:31.759 --> 00:00:36.890
We are going to look at clips of Chris Christie's
town hall that he did yesterday announcing

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:40.070
his candidacy running against Trump.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.400
And it's after watching this town hall.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.370
It's clearer than ever to me.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:51.850
If I were voting in the Republican primary,
if I knew a Republican would be president,

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.380
it would be Chris Christie that I would support.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:58.640
And this is not about glorifying or glamorizing
the guy.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.640
But he's willing to tell what should be pretty
uncontroversial truths.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.640
He doesn't equivocate when he's asked about
Trump and say, well, I'm not talking.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.939
I'm here focused on me, not on Trump.

00:01:09.939 --> 00:01:13.460
No, he understands you've got to go against
Trump.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.729
And this was a very solid town hall.

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:21.640
If more Republicans were like Chris Christie,
we would have a much better country than we

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.900
do with people like Trump and Marjorie Taylor
GREENE and Lauren Boebert and these sorts

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.140
of lunatics.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.860
Here's Chris Christie going right after Trump.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:30.860
He's not afraid.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:37.290
Speaker 3: A lonely self consumed.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.799
Self-serving.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.470
Mirror hog.

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:44.579
He is not a leader.

00:01:44.579 --> 00:01:47.189
Well, let me be clear.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:54.329
In case I have not been already the person
I am talking about.

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:56.830
Who is obsessed with the mirror.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:59.220
Who never admits a mistake.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.080
Who never admits a fault.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.680
And who always find someone else.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:09.759
And something else to blame for whatever goes
wrong but finds every reason to take credit

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:12.620
for anything that goes right.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:16.100
Is Donald Trump.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:22.280
And if we don't have that conversation with
you.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.280
We don't deserve.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.319
To ask for your vote.

00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:27.640
Speaker 1: I completely agree.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:32.340
Nikki Haley won't even say anything other
than, Well, I'm a woman and I'm younger and

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.530
I'm a person of color.

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:38.430
And Tim Scott says there's going to be a contrast,
but I'm not making this about other candidates.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.910
Now, an audience member during this town hall
asked Chris Christie.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:46.400
If Trump's indicted and you're president,
will you pardon him?

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.950
When DeSantis was asked about this.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:50.989
He basically said yes.

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:56.360
Chris Christie, on the other hand, is saying
almost certainly not with a little bit of

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.490
equivocation, but almost certainly not.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.380
Speaker 3: If Donald Trump is indicted.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.069
Speaker 4: And you become president.

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:09.670
Speaker 3: Will you pardon him?

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.166
Well, I. I have to tell you the truth.

00:03:12.166 --> 00:03:17.159
I can't completely answer that until I know
what he was charged with and convicted of.

00:03:17.159 --> 00:03:21.060
Okay, So but but I'm not going to dodge the
answer.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.140
Okay.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.920
But I will tell you, as a prosecutor, if I
believe someone has gotten a full and fair

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:33.939
trial in front of a jury of their peers and
especially someone in public life who committed

00:03:33.939 --> 00:03:39.530
those crimes when they held a public trust,
I can't imagine pardoning them.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.590
Speaker 1: Okay.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:46.510
So I'm hearing that is almost certainly not
not a perfect answer, but a thousand times

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:49.569
better than the answer given by Ron DeSantis.

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:55.950
Chris Christie did had on face what he considers
the biggest mistake of his political career,

00:03:55.950 --> 00:04:02.379
which was that some of the people working
for him had that insane situation where they

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:07.040
diverted traffic off the George Washington
Bridge as political punishment, I believe

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.819
it was to the mayor of Fort Lee, New Jersey,
although I don't now remember 100%.

00:04:11.819 --> 00:04:18.350
Obviously, Chris Christie is going to minimize
the degree to which he was the one at fault,

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.269
but he's taking responsibility.

00:04:20.269 --> 00:04:25.570
I just wish more Republicans talked to this
directly because they just you can't get a

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:28.720
straight answer out of almost any of these
clowns.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:33.130
Speaker 3: The biggest mistake I made public
life was I put a few people into a position

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:37.570
of authority at the Port Authority of New
York and New Jersey, who went on a frolicking

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:43.360
detour to divert traffic off the George Washington
Bridge without telling me, without me knowing

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.449
anything about it.

00:04:44.449 --> 00:04:52.850
They used my power and my authority to play
a fraternity prank, and it costs me a lot.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:55.510
It cost me credibility.

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:56.780
It humiliated me publicly.

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:00.789
And I should have never put those people in
that position.

00:05:00.789 --> 00:05:01.949
The biggest mistake I made.

00:05:01.949 --> 00:05:03.160
There you go.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.160
Biggest mistake.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.820
Speaker 1: Chris Christie also addressing
the claim by Donald Trump that if he were

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:12.980
president, he would end the Russia Ukraine
war in 24 hours.

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:16.729
Chris Christie pointing out the way he would
end it is by giving everything to Russia.

00:05:16.729 --> 00:05:22.750
Speaker 3: And now I heard him say if we made
it president again, he would settle the Ukraine

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.419
war in 24 hours.

00:05:24.419 --> 00:05:26.990
Did you hear that one?

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:27.990
That's a beauty.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:35.500
That's really in a career of complete falsehoods
that makes the top five.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.680
But let's give him the benefit of the doubt.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.520
Let's say Donald Trump could settle it in
24 hours.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.400
Let me tell you how he would.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.521
He'd give Ukraine to Russia and he said it.

00:05:45.521 --> 00:05:46.930
He said it on television.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.320
He said, let's see it.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.699
And he said, well, Russia's a winner with
Ukraine anyway.

00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:53.960
So what's the difference?

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:56.900
That's how it settled in 24 hours.

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:59.039
He calls Alinsky and say, Hey, guess what?

00:05:59.039 --> 00:06:01.400
Time to raise the Russian flag up on the pole.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:02.400
We're out of here.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.730
Speaker 1: There are no other Republican candidates
willing to say this.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:10.889
They just aren't willing to do it, whether
they believe it or not, I don't know.

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:13.240
But Chris Christie is at least willing to
say this stuff.

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:17.870
And it is abundantly clear to me that there
is going to be one guy on the stage with Trump

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.630
if they get that far who is not going to be
pulling punches.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:22.330
Everybody else is pulling punches.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:23.530
Chris Christie is not pulling punches.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:27.560
Here is Chris Christie breaking out the Trump
impression on day one of his campaign.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:33.230
Speaker 3: It was a mistake in 2016 not to
confront Donald Trump early.

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:37.669
True, because I knew that so much of what
he said was complete baloney.

00:06:37.669 --> 00:06:38.669
Like I knew it.

00:06:38.669 --> 00:06:44.030
I am going to build the greatest, most wonderful
wall across the entire Mexico border, and

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:46.330
Mexico is going to pay for it.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:54.180
Well, like I knew as someone who had governed
that that was complete bull, but I was like,

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:57.300
Yeah, people aren't going to believe that.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.979
They're not going to believe that mistake.

00:07:01.979 --> 00:07:02.979
It was a mistake.

00:07:02.979 --> 00:07:04.930
Speaker 1: And he's completely correct.

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:08.349
And he points out other bogus claims that
Trump has made.

00:07:08.349 --> 00:07:10.349
He talks about debt and deficit here.

00:07:10.349 --> 00:07:14.260
And again, this isn't the Chris Christie cheerleading
segment.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:20.070
It's there is something notably different
about Chris Christie compared to all the other

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:22.650
candidates and how they are relating to the
issues.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:26.039
Notice that there isn't any anti-woke stuff
here.

00:07:26.039 --> 00:07:30.850
At least he's talking about moderately real
issues.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:34.460
Here he is about national debt and pointing
out Trump's lies there as well.

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:39.160
Speaker 3: Reason this is going to be different
this time, sir, is because at least one of

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.160
us.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:44.500
Is going to call him on the fact that eight
years ago he stood on the stage in New Hampshire

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:48.400
and said he was going to balance the budget
in four years.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:54.460
And he left with the biggest deficit of any
president in American history.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:08:00.639
He said he was going to eliminate the national
debt in eight years.

00:08:00.639 --> 00:08:02.380
Speaker 1: Trump did say that.

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:08.379
Speaker 3: He added $3 trillion to the national
debt in four years.

00:08:08.379 --> 00:08:11.830
Speaker 1: So a very, very strong town hall
overall.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:16.190
It'll be interesting to see whether this moves
the needle at all in terms of polling, which

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:19.120
right now is not great for Chris Christie.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.050
One last.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:22.490
Clip from this.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:28.909
Chris Christie made the claim during the town
hall that if Biden had been running against

00:08:28.909 --> 00:08:36.459
someone different in 2020, Biden would have
lost that Biden was a poor candidate but won

00:08:36.459 --> 00:08:40.610
because so many people so acutely dislike
Donald Trump.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:44.360
And it's certainly possible that that is true.

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:45.360
It's possible.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:46.990
Speaker 3: Let me be very clear.

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:49.149
I am going out there to take out Donald Trump.

00:08:49.149 --> 00:08:55.100
But here's why I want to win and I don't want
him to win.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.100
And guess what?

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:01.060
If you put the Santas and Haley and Pence.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.140
And Tim Scott.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.690
That's it.

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:04.790
I'll stop there.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.860
A truth serum.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.760
They tell you the same thing.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:09.760
Here's the difference.

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:10.760
Here's the difference.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:14.000
You have to put me on truth serum to tell
you.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.000
Okay.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:20.040
So that's why there are not multiple lanes
to the Republican nomination.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.230
That is a political science professor's dream.

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.149
There is one thing.

00:09:24.149 --> 00:09:25.149
Yep.

00:09:25.149 --> 00:09:27.640
It's the Republican nomination and he's in
front of it.

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:31.160
And if you want to win, you better go right
through.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.279
Because let me guarantee you something.

00:09:32.279 --> 00:09:33.990
From knowing him for 22 years, everybody.

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:35.670
He had to go through me.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:43.089
He's going to try to go through Ron and Nikki
and Tim and anybody else who stands in his

00:09:43.089 --> 00:09:44.089
way.

00:09:44.089 --> 00:09:45.089
Speaker 1: All right.

00:09:45.089 --> 00:09:46.089
So Chris Christie gets it.

00:09:46.089 --> 00:09:47.650
Chris Christie understands what's going on.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:51.350
Trump's not a good candidate, but Trump is
leading the Republican nomination.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:53.450
The path to the nomination is through Trump.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:58.459
It's not taking your 2% like Nikki Haley or
sorry, 4% like Nikki Haley, or 2% like Tim

00:09:58.459 --> 00:09:59.459
Scott.

00:09:59.459 --> 00:10:04.209
And just talking about how you're going to
be positive and whatever the path is through

00:10:04.209 --> 00:10:05.209
Trump.

00:10:05.209 --> 00:10:06.540
And the question is whether Chris Christie
will be able to do it.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.540
I don't know.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.620
I'm curious to see what polling looks like
in two weeks.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:14.080
In the meantime, all sorts of people reacting
to Chris Christie's candidacy just by talking

00:10:14.080 --> 00:11:28.560
about his weight.

